A||||5||Shaun41178||1-1 w/ stang and lost to C4 Vette||||9
Z||000000||Shaun41178||11-11-1999||01:39 AM||||Well my unbeaten streak has finally gone to the cr@pper. Perhaps because I ran into some reasonable competition tonight. Well maybe<P><BR>Anyway cruising tonight and i get off the freeway and then just driving down a fairly busy road when a ford truck like a Ranger and then a foxbody Mustang convertible goes flyin bye. They were apparantly fooling around with each other so I let them go. As the Mustang drove by I could hear his exhasut over my radio with the windows up. Yea real loud. Anyway I appraoch a red light and both of them are at the light and I pull in behind the truck but never get fully stopped as the light turned green before I got there. Truck shoots off but the Mustang gets stuck behind a car and has to keep it slow. I am passing on the left of the stang when the car he was behind turns into a parking lot and I hear the stang get on it hard so I do as well. We went from about a 25 mph roll up to about 65 or so and I had him the whole way and when I shut down he was at my rear qtr panel but he stayed on it and passed me and as he did he gave me the look like what the hell is in that thing. I let him go but he gets caught at a light up ahead and no traffic. I decide to try him from a light. I get next to him and his exhasut is really loud. He defintately had exhaust work done. Here is the conversation:<P>Me: Whats in that thing?<BR>Him: A 302<BR>Me: Any mods?<BR>Him: No<BR>Me: Wanna run it?<BR>Him: Sure.<P>Now i knew this guy was lying about mods cause he hung with me pretty well from the roll just a bit earlier. So the light turns green and I hit the nitrous right off the line. hardly any spin for me which I thought was odd cause when I usually hit nitrous off the line on the street I peel for about 10 feet or so. But nothing here at all. This guy pulled a car on me before first gear was over. When I hit second he has about another half car but he has stopped pulling on me but I am not gaining. He shuts it down and I pull up along side and give him the thumbs up. He does the same and just keeps on driving ahead as I try to let him know that I am turning as I had my blinker on for a long time hoping he would turn to so we could talk. It makes me wonder about how fast this stang jumped me off the line. It seems like he had gears or something like that. I mean this was a convertible. Stock at best was like low 15's right since they had those auto tranny's? Did any come with manual tranny's? I mean I smoked a SN-95 GT badly from a roll a week ago and then I lose to a so-called Fox-body convertible? Sounds fishy.<P>Well upset about my first loss i continue onward and look for revenge. Well wouldn't you know a C4 Vette goes by in the otehr direction so I bust a U-turn and catch up. Catch him at a light but had cars up ahead so I rev it to get his attention. Sure enough he bites. This guy is about 25-30 I would say. I later found out he was on his way to the Nudey Bar. Well this guy tries to go with traffic ahead about 100 feet or so and I wanted no part of that since it wouldn't last long before we would have to shut down. He never slowed down either as I tried pulling alongside and then slowing down hoping he would do the same. Anyway he turns off on this road which he chooses to be one of the crappiest roads in town but lucky for me he chooses the curb lane. Tons of potholes in the curb lanes here. Anyway I pull up alongside and I get a tad ahead and I hear him punch it and so do I. Well it was about even for like 2 seconds. Then after that he pulled like 8 cars on me in no time. I mean as soon as he hit like 3rd gear or something he was gone. I felt stupid for even wasting this guys time. i thought this guy was running nitrous or something by how fast he walked me. Anyway I am following him and he pulls into a parking lot(Nudey Bar) so I follow. He gets out and I begin talking with the guy. He says that it is a 92 Vette. I immediately knew he had the Lt-1. He said he had like 324 hp cause he installed a chip. LT-1 Vettes came with 300 hp from the factory right? He said he has an auto tranny as well. <BR>Anyways the guy was cool and I gave him a thumbs up and wished him luck in the Nudey Bar.<P>Now I am not going to try and make excuses here. My car was running great but I am a tad dissappointed that I lost tonight. Anyways Usually before I go out I put some warm bottle around the nitrous bottle to help bring the pressure up as the temps this time of season at night are in the 50's. Anyways I didn't do that so I am sure my bottle pressure was way down. Take the bottle out of the trunk and when I take the nitrous feed line off almost no gas came rushing out of the line. It was a small amount of air and it wasn't even cold, however it was under pressure but not like how it is when there is a lot of pressure in the line. So I ask myself if the bottle could be empty. Get the scale out and sure enough the bottle only weighed 16 pounds. I only had like 1-2 pounds left in the bottle. Damnit I thought. I wonder how I would have done against that vette if I had a full bottle and good pressure. I know I would have smoked that stang for sure but i wonder about the vette. Man this sucks but I guess it had to happen sometime. But tonight of all nights when I race my first vette my nitrous was not up to where it should have been for trying to tackle a vette. Oh well like I said I am not trying to make excuses but I won't let it happen again and I will be ready next time for sure. <P>Later and thanks for reading all of this as I know it is long.||||reg||9
Z||000001||ChadMan||11-11-1999||09:54 AM||||Don't be sorry.  "Shaun's Street-Racing Chronicles" are one of the things I enjoy best about the Forum.<P>I got a good laugh out of the Vette guy being on his way to the nudey bar - I pictured Al Bundy in a borrowed Vette with dark glasses and a leisure suit.  Ha!<P>(Not that there's anything wrong with nudey bars, mind you, or the nice young ladies who work there.)||||reg||10
Z||000002||88 Fiero||11-11-1999||11:16 AM||||Don't feel bad Shaun...it happens once in awhile...just think of it next time you see this guys...they on for a surprise!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT Bastard||11-11-1999||02:19 PM||||Sounds like you got a pretty quick Fiero, but you've got to try running it without nitrous at the track sometime.  I'm sure you're fellow auto guys are curious what it'll run natually aspirated.  I've been turning my attention away from my LT1, and towards to my little Fiero V6 lately, so I'm looking for ideas to make it faster.  I must admit though, I'm not a fan of nitrous.  The idea of having temporary horsepower that you need to refill doesn't seem right.  That, combined with the fact that it kills engines... Anyhow, see ya later man.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Shaun41178||11-12-1999||03:11 PM||||i have run my car at the track naturally aspirated many times, however I don't know if I have ever posted them up here in the forum.  I know they are not on my webpage.  <P>Anyway without nitrous my car runs 16.1-16.4.  Its pretty consistent as all I have to do is put my foot to the floor.  I think a shift kit might be able to get me into the 15's n/a.  Plus with the cooler weather now if I couls mangae to get lucky and shave .1 off my best time I will be in the 15's on a n/a auto Fiero.  Not bad I think.<P>0-60 comes in just under 8 seconds without nitrous.  Usually around 7.8-7.9||||reg||1
Z||000005||superXmotorsports||11-13-1999||06:52 PM||||I had 2 races last night w/ unusual opponents.  #1 stoplight race with new 'Extreme' S10 pickup.  Took him by about 2 cars in a block or so.  #2 Highway race against MX6 pulled him from about 80 to 110 by about 5 cars.  Just some more race stories from the Fiero underworld.<BR>(They were lucky I was in my stock 87 GT)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
